{"id":"s4","level":5,"levelName":"Structure and style","n":7,"of":10,"title":"How it's done","titleHe":"תֹּאַר הַפֹּעַל","goal":"Modify a verb — with an adverb, or with a preposition and a noun.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Hebrew has fewer true adverbs than English and makes up the difference with בְּ plus an abstract noun: בְּשֶׁקֶט quietly, literally in quiet."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"הוּא מְדַבֵּר מַהֵר.","en":"He speaks quickly."},{"he":"הִיא כָּתְבָה בִּזְהִירוּת.","en":"She wrote carefully."},{"he":"אֲנִי מַכִּיר אוֹתוֹ הֵיטֵב.","en":"I know him well."}]},{"type":"tip","body":"טוֹב is an adjective doing adverb duty in speech — הוּא כּוֹתֵב טוֹב. In writing you'd want הֵיטֵב."}],"vocab":[{"he":"מַהֵר","en":"quickly","translit":"maher"},{"he":"לְאַט","en":"slowly","translit":"le'at"},{"he":"הֵיטֵב","en":"well, thoroughly","translit":"heitev"},{"he":"מְאוֹד","en":"very","translit":"me'od"},{"he":"תָּמִיד","en":"always","translit":"tamid"},{"he":"לִפְעָמִים","en":"sometimes","translit":"lif'amim"},{"he":"כְּבָר","en":"already","translit":"kvar"},{"he":"בְּשֶׁקֶט","en":"quietly","translit":"besheket"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["quickly","might","teaches","misses, longs for"],"correct":0,"prompt":"מַהֵר","translit":"maher"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["slowly","juice","inheritance, estate","lawyer"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לְאַט","translit":"le'at"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["in fact","strange","polite, courteous","well, thoroughly"],"correct":3,"prompt":"הֵיטֵב","translit":"heitev"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["commentary, meaning","tail","floor","very"],"correct":3,"prompt":"מְאוֹד","translit":"me'od"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["always","conclusion","tries","blessing"],"correct":0,"prompt":"תָּמִיד","translit":"tamid"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["mother","sometimes","bride","river"],"correct":1,"prompt":"לִפְעָמִים","translit":"lif'amim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["goat","already","gives","a minority"],"correct":1,"prompt":"כְּבָר","translit":"kvar"},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"אֲנִי ___ אוֹתוֹ הֵיטֵב.","en":"I know him well.","options":["מַכִּיר","הֵיטֵב","מְאוֹד","לְאַט"],"correct":0,"full":"אֲנִי מַכִּיר אוֹתוֹ הֵיטֵב."},{"type":"listen","q":"Which word did you hear?","options":["מְאוֹד","לְאַט","מַהֵר","לִפְעָמִים"],"correct":1,"say":"לְאַט","he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["מַהֵר","quickly"],["לְאַט","slowly"],["הֵיטֵב","well, thoroughly"],["מְאוֹד","very"],["תָּמִיד","always"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “sometimes”?","options":["לִפְעָמִים","חֲנֻכָּה","צַוָּאר","עֶצֶם"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “already”?","options":["תִּשְׁעִים","מֵאָה","כְּבָר","יָכוֹל"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “quietly”?","options":["מַרְגִּישׁ","עַיֵּן שָׁם","כְּאֵב","בְּשֶׁקֶט"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “very”?","options":["נָחָשׁ","מְאוֹד","מָה","אֵם"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"cloze","sentence":"הִיא כָּתְבָה ___.","en":"She wrote carefully.","options":["תָּמִיד","בִּזְהִירוּת","לִפְעָמִים","לְאַט"],"correct":1,"full":"הִיא כָּתְבָה בִּזְהִירוּת."},{"type":"type","q":"Write “already” in Hebrew","answer":"כְּבָר","hint":"kvar"}]}